Based on the search results, here's information about setting up DeepSeek with OpenCode:

## Setup Methods

There are two main approaches to configure DeepSeek with OpenCode:

### 1. Using the Built-in `/connect` Flow (Recommended)

Start `opencode`, type `/connect`, search for `deepseek`, select the provider, enter your DeepSeek API key, and then choose DeepSeek V4 Pro.

### 2. Manual Configuration File Setup

OpenCode connects to OpenAI-compatible APIs through the @ai-sdk/openai-compatible adapter, with the base URL https://api.deepseek.com/v1.

A custom DeepSeek provider configuration uses the {env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY} syntax to pull the key from your environment instead of hard-coding it.

A typical configuration in `opencode.json` looks like:

```json
{
  "provider": {
    "deepseek": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "DeepSeek",
      "options": {
[REDACTED]"baseURL": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1",
[REDACTED]"apiKey": "{env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}"
      },
      "models": {
[REDACTED]"deepseek-chat": { "name": "DeepSeek Chat" },
[REDACTED]"deepseek-reasoner": { "name": "DeepSeek Reasoner" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Environment Variable Setup

Export the API key first by running:
```bash
export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=your-deepseek-api-key
```

## Model Options

Start with deepseek-v4-pro, which is a Mixture-of-Experts model with a 1M-token context window and frontier coding scores at sub-dollar token pricing. Drop to deepseek-v4-flash when running heavy volume to shave cost for a small quality trade.

